Implementation reasoning — /learn codebase learning path (spec 20260609-230029)

WHY THE ARCHITECTURE:
- All GitHub access + heuristics live in src/app/services/ (not the view) so
  they are unit-testable without a request context and the view stays a thin
  HTTP adapter. The unused controllers/ package was intentionally left alone.
- A single AnalysisError(code, message, status) type centralizes the spec's
  status-code map (400/404/413/422/429/502). The view is one try/except.

URL PARSER (repository_url.py):
- Deliberately strict: only https + github.com, root or /tree/<branch>/<path>.
  Strictness is the security gate — it prevents constructing ambiguous API
  calls. Branch is single-segment by design because tree/<a>/<b>/<c> is
  inherently ambiguous between branch=a path=b/c and branch=a/b path=c; we
  document "first segment is the branch". .git suffix is root-only.
- normalized_url lowercases owner/repo (GitHub is case-insensitive there) so
  the cache key is stable; scope path is preserved verbatim.

GITHUB CLIENT (github_repository_client.py):
- Private repos are rejected by the analyzer via metadata.private even though
  the client can read them with a token — satisfies "never analyze private".
- Rate limit detected from 429 OR (403 + X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0).
- Timeouts/connection errors -> 502 upstream (never leak exception text).
- get_file_content returns None (not raise) for binary/oversized/undecodable —
  those are "skip this file" signals, not request failures.
- Per-request budget (REPOSITORY_ANALYSIS_MAX_API_REQUESTS) prevents fan-out.
- FakeGitHubRepositoryClient mirrors the surface from a CPython/IDLE fixture so
  TestingConfig and Playwright never hit the network; it recognizes only the
  stable fixture URL and 404s everything else (handy for the not-found path).

ANALYZER (repository_analysis.py):
- Deterministic by construction (no LLM/randomness) so results are reproducible
  and cacheable. 8 ordered categories; tie-break is (score desc, category asc,
  depth asc, path asc) — fully total, verified by a test that feeds reversed
  tree input and asserts identical ordering.
- Cache is keyed (normalized_url, commit_sha): re-analyzing after a new commit
  yields fresh guidance; same commit returns cached WITHOUT fetching the tree
  or files (the expensive part) — asserted by call-count test.
- Duplicate-insert race: catch IntegrityError -> rollback -> re-query -> serve
  existing as cached:true (asserted by pre-seeding a colliding row).
- Entry-point files (only) are fetched to sharpen their rationale using cheap
  signals (if __name__ == __main__, def main, create_app/Flask). Excerpts are
  intentionally NOT surfaced — the locked Step-1 contract has no excerpt field.

VITE MANIFEST FIX (vite_manifest.py):
- base.html previously hard-coded assets/main.js|css which never exist after a
  hashed build, so production shipped no JS/CSS (latent bug the spec mandated
  fixing). Helper reads .vite/manifest.json (Vite 5) and resolves src/main.ts
  to hashed JS+CSS; falls back to legacy names if no manifest so it never 500s.

FRONTEND:
- Island renders all repo-provided strings as React text (no
  dangerouslySetInnerHTML); a test injects an <img onerror> string and asserts
  no <img> element is created. initialAnalysis renders saved pages with zero
  fetches (asserted). Field names mirror the backend exactly — one contract,
  no ad-hoc transforms.

TOOLING NOTE:
- The mypy PRE-COMMIT hook checks staged tests too and runs in an isolated env;
  added types-requests + pytest to additional_dependencies. script/typecheck
  only checks src/, so it did not catch the test-typing requirements — worth
  remembering for future loops.

